<title>UK: Rolls-Royce in deal with Flying Colours.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce in deal with Flying Colours.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and aerospace group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Thursday its unit Rolls-Royce Aero Engines Services Ltd won an eight-year engine overhaul contract worth 12 million stg from British airline Flying Colours.</p>
<p>Rolls-Royce said Manchester-based Flying Colours would begin commercial operations between March and May this year with four Boeing 757 airliners powered by Rolls-Royce engines.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
